  "summary": {
    "plain": "In its first results, the 250 kg DAMA/LIBRA detector saw the same yearly rise and fall as DAMA/NaI. DAMA says the two experiments together support dark matter in the galactic halo at 8.2 standard deviations.",
    "technical": "First DAMA/LIBRA annual-modulation result: exposure 0.53 ton yr; 0.82 ton yr combined with DAMA/NaI. The abstract states that neither systematic effects nor side reactions can account for the observed modulation amplitude while satisfying all requirements of the signature."
